text.paragraph:
[see
  Use in Specific Populations

                              (

                           8.1

                              )
                           ].

Counsel patients, their caregivers, and families that AEDs, including valproic acid, may increase the risk of suicidal thoughts and behavior and to be alert for the emergence or worsening of symptoms of depression, any unusual changes in mood or behavior, or the emergence of suicidal thoughts, behavior, or thoughts about self-harm. Instruct patients, caregivers, and families to report behaviors of concern immediately to the healthcare providers [see 

                           Warnings and Precautions

                               (

                           5.7

                              )
                           ].

Instruct patients that a fever associated with other organ system involvement (rash, lymphadenopathy, etc.) may be drug-related and should be reported to the physician immediately [see 

                           Warnings and Precautions

                               (

                           5.12

                              )
                           ].
